<title>USA: Ford U.S. '96 profit sharing rises.</title>
<headline>Ford U.S. '96 profit sharing rises.</headline>
<dateline>DEARBORN, Mich. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co said Wednesday its U.S. employees will receive profit sharing checks averaging $1,800, up slightly from the average $1,700 paid out a year ago.</p>
<p>Ford Chairman and Chief Executive Officer Alex Trotman said the checks will be distributed March 5 to about 163,000 workers.</p>
<p>&quot;While our business results in 1996 were somewhat improved over 1995, we must continue to drive down costs while achieving high levels of quality if we are to remain competitive,&quot; he said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ford's checks are more than the $300 that General Motors Corp said Tuesday it would pay to its U.S. union workers. Chrysler Corp's U.S. workers will receive an average of $7,900 in 1996 profit sharing.</p>
</text>
